.DS_Store
.build/
build/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
DerivedData/

# `.claude/` is ignored whole: Claude Code keeps `worktrees/` (linked worktree
# checkouts, which git would otherwise add as embedded repositories) and
# `settings.local.json` (named in `.worktreeinclude`) there, and nothing in
# this repository creates either.
/.claude/

# Plans and specs are a record of decisions being made, not of what the program
# is; the project's pages live in Core. `docs/superpowers/` falls under this.
/docs

# The superpowers skills write brainstorm mockups here, working material for
# one conversation.
/.superpowers/

# Xcode writes `.swiftpm/` the first time it opens this package, and what lands
# there is two genres in one directory. `xcode/xcshareddata/xcschemes/Helm.xcscheme`
# is shared by design — it says how the package builds and runs, it is the same
# for whoever opens it, so the line below leaves it un-ignored; no commit tracks it
# yet. The rest is one person's window state: `UserInterfaceState.xcuserstate` and `xcschememanagement.plist`,
# both under a folder named after the account, both rewritten whenever a window
# moves. Ignoring only the per-user halves is the line `*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/`
# already draws above, rather than a second policy for the same question.
.swiftpm/**/xcuserdata/

# Internal agent rules and secrets stay out of this repo: `CLAUDE.local.md`
# and `AGENTS.md` are symlinks to `<Core>/<project>/CLAUDE.md`.
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
